# Written by titanfall2vr. One line per headset this build has seen.
# The geometry is remembered because the resolution has to be set before
# OpenXR can report it. `scale` is that headset's OWN resolution setting;
# a headset seen for the FIRST time starts at the shipped default, which
# is deliberately below the per-eye height the runtime asks for: the
# widened buffer at 1.00 is about twice a 4K frame and no GPU check is
# made. Raise it in the config menu if you have the headroom.
# Delete this file to forget every headset.
#
# THIS COPY IS A SEED, not a recording. It was measured on a Meta Quest 3
# through Virtual Desktop's VDXR runtime, and it exists so that a Quest 3
# user's FIRST launch already knows the panel geometry instead of deriving
# it -- which is the badly magnified first minute in KNOWN-ISSUES 8.
#
# It only helps if your fingerprint matches the line below, and the
# fingerprint includes the per-eye resolution your runtime asks for, which
# changes with Virtual Desktop's quality setting. If it does not match, the
# file is ignored and your headset is learned the usual way: no harm, no
# benefit. Nothing here is personal to the machine it was measured on.
#
# The field after `scale` is a field-of-view scale, and it is deliberately
# 0 here. A derived one is exactly what KNOWN-ISSUES 17 suspects, and a
# seeded file has no business shipping somebody else's.
#
# fields: recW recH tanW tanH scale fovScale fingerprint
active 0
headset 3072 3264 1.37638 1.27325 0.7500 0.0000 Meta Quest 3|VirtualDesktopXR|3072x3264|2.215x2.394
